The retired Forgejo tracker-ci.yml was a dedicated lightweight job (~15s). The
Woodpecker port folded tracker validation into the general per-PR gate but left
hook-tests + prepare-git (no `when:` -> always-on) and dco (all PRs) running for
a tracker-ops-only PR. Those four container steps (each apt/pip-installing in a
fresh python:3.11-bookworm) outran do_sync's CI-poll timeout, so every auto-sync
PR timed out and no tracker ops could reach GitHub dev.

Add a shared `non_tracker_paths` path filter (include ** / exclude
.agent/tracker/** + .agent/tracker-workspace/**) to hook-tests, prepare-git, and
dco. A tracker-sync PR now runs ONLY tracker-validate -> one fast step, well under
the poll timeout. Code / docs PRs are unaffected (they match the filter). Skipping
dco for tracker PRs is safe: do_sync already writes a Signed-off-by trailer
(sync.py:1520-1531), verified present on the pushed sync commit.

Config-only (.woodpecker + CHANGELOG); smart-test selects 0 tests.

